  "scope": "Actual Gaussian outer marginal nu=J.snd admits a dense genuine smooth-compact gradient graph, is closable, and has closed closure. No literal Tf graph membership, arbitrary rough L2 smoothing estimate, Gamma/half-turn/main/errors/cost or actual-input composition is proved.",
  "independent_reviewer": "phase_source_reviewer_20261005",
  "signatures": [
    {
      "full_declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianMarginalGradient.gaussian_marginal_gradient_closable",
      "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/FunctionalInequalities/GaussianMarginalGradient.lean",
      "signature_text": "theorem gaussian_marginal_gradient_closable\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    (μ : Measure E) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ] {η : ℝ} (hη : 0 < η) :\n    let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n      (fun p : E × E => (p.1, p.1 + Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n    let ν := J.snd\n    ∃ D : Lp ℝ 2 ν →ₗ.[ℝ] Lp E 2 ν,\n      Dense (D.domain : Set (Lp ℝ 2 ν)) ∧ D.IsClosable ∧ D.closure.IsClosed ∧\n      ∀ (u : Lp ℝ 2 ν) (v : Lp E 2 ν), (u,v) ∈ D.graph ↔\n        ∃ f : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ ∞ f ∧ HasCompactSupport f ∧\n          u =ᵐ[ν] f ∧ v =ᵐ[ν] gradient f\n",
      "signature_lf_sha256": "d7273526caa94ec518b790626edb6b289bdabfdd1104a196cd2e8eb110211e81",
      "signature_raw_sha256": "2cf564dbef4930610930618249797ea292c9224f3bfa17dec61285c47234e2f8",
      "LF_bytes": 697
    }
  ],
